# Line endings — LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# ## Why this file exists
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` was set on this machine and nothing declared what the
# repo wanted, so the working tree drifted into a mix: 7 of 44 files in
# `server/` were CRLF and the rest LF, including the five an agent edits most —
# actions.mjs, airouter.mjs, jobs.mjs, providers.mjs, workspace.mjs.
#
# That is not cosmetic here. An agent edits by matching exact text, and a
# multi-line match written with LF cannot match a file stored with CRLF. On
# 2026-09-04 a session gave up on a one-word change for exactly this reason and
# left a comment saying so — `providers.mjs` kept `attachments: false` under a
# paragraph explaining that it should be true and could not be edited. The flag
# then contradicted its own documentation until someone did it by hand.
#
# So the cost of the mix is not ugly diffs, it is an agent that cannot reliably
# edit the files it works in, failing in a way that reads as a tooling quirk
# rather than a repo setting.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf per path, which is why this fixes it without
# anyone changing their global git config — and it holds for the next machine
# too, which a config setting would not.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text. Several of these contain 0x0D
# bytes and a naive CRLF scan reports them as text files needing conversion.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
